# Git: main only

## Studio / Builder / platform control-plane

- Default working branch: **`main`**.
- When asked to commit/push/deploy these changes: commit on `main`, `git fetch` + integrate if behind, then `git push origin main`.
- Treat “deploy” as Vyom / `indobase.in`.
- Do not commit, push, or deploy via **`staging`** / `indobase.fun` unless the user names that host explicitly.

## Production

- Before pushing `main`: `git fetch origin` and integrate if behind (`git pull --rebase origin main`).
- Do not force-push `main` unless explicitly requested.
- Production rollout uses SHA tags on `.249` (see `indobase-prod-redeploy.mdc`).

## Other work

- Unrelated one-off branches only if the user names one.
- Marketing (`apps/www`) and infra-only docs follow `main` unless the user names another branch.
